# Backend Rules

- Validate all external input at trust boundaries (Pydantic models, idempotency keys, JWT claims).
- Keep business rules out of transport handlers; use `app/services/` for domain logic.
- Use the repository's existing error model (`app/core/errors.py` typed `AppError` codes).
- Use tenant-scoped queries: `business_id` must come from verified access token claims only.
- Use idempotency keys with fingerprint verification; never sniff error-message text for codes.
- Add or update tests for behavior changes.
- Do not introduce a dependency without justification (pin in `requirements.txt` or `dev-requirements.txt`).
- Settings uses `extra="forbid"` — only declared fields may appear in `.env`.
- JWT expiry is configurable via `jwt_expiry_minutes`; do not hardcode 480 minutes.
- `/metrics` requires bearer token authentication.
